# Log files are local diagnostic output, never committed. They contain
# participant ids, staff ids, and IP addresses — identifying data that belongs
# in a running deployment, not in version control.
#
# This directory is tracked (via this file alone) rather than created at
# runtime, so a fresh clone has somewhere to write to and `logs/` never appears
# as an untracked directory in `git status`.
#
# Kept here rather than in the repository root because the root `.gitignore`
# covers the whole project, and this rule is entirely about `backend/logs`.
*
!.gitignore
